    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕmŏrātus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		memoro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a</i>
			
			<i>mentioning, relating; a mention, relation</i>
			(ante-class. and post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">istaec lepida sunt memoratui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 1, 1, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">estne hoc miserum memoratu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Cist. 2, 1, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parva et levia memoratu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 32</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 2, 73</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumen memoratu dignum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 10, 15, § 95</span></i>
			.</div>
